    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The flood response revealed how a state actor's initial maneuvering created a pivotal upstream concession. A head of state, acting as a catalyst of post-flood change, oversaw the visible presidential engagement in disaster zones. Meanwhile, the instrument of state intervention coordinated a rescue operation, addressing the infrastructure damage caused by the embankment failure. This sequence highlights the leverage points where systems pivot under pressure.",
